body:
KeyedQuery keeps every entry until the parent clears the whole cache, so parents cannot drop one key or prune the retained set when selection or routing changes.

Add `forget` and `retainOnly` to KeyedQuery. `forget` removes one entry, and `retainOnly` keeps the supplied keys without fetching missing ones or changing retained entries. Both preserve request generations, so a completion for a removed entry is ignored.

Add `refetch` to Query and KeyedQuery. It starts a new Fetch even when one is pending, keeps available data on screen, and ignores the superseded completion. On a settled entry it behaves like `revalidateOrLoad`. It matters when a KeyedQuery's custom `toKey` maps new arguments to a pending entry, where `loadIfMissing` and `revalidateOrLoad` leave the old Fetch running. The name leaves `replace` free for writing data into the cache, which #1727 also asks for.

Update the API Cache Query example to keep the details of the two most recently opened posts. Reopening a recent post reads its retained entry without a fetch, and opening a third evicts the oldest.

```ts
const RECENT_POST_LIMIT = 2

const postDetails = postQuery.lift<Model, Message>({
  parentField: 'postDetails',
  toParentMessage: message => Message.GotPostMessage({ message }),
})

// Keep the most recent posts, then fetch the selected one when missing.
ClickedPost: ({ postId }) => {
  const nextRecentPostIds = pipe(
    model.recentPostIds,
    Array.filter(recentPostId => recentPostId !== postId),
    Array.prepend(postId),
    Array.take(RECENT_POST_LIMIT),
  )

  return Update.combine(
    modifyFields(model, {
      maybeSelectedPostId: () => Option.some(postId),
      recentPostIds: () => nextRecentPostIds,
    }),
    [
      postDetails.retainOnly(
        Array.map(nextRecentPostIds, recentPostId => ({
          postId: recentPostId,
        })),
      ),
      postDetails.loadIfMissing({ postId }),
    ],
  )
},

// Starts a new Fetch even when one is pending.
// Retained data stays visible and the older completion is ignored.
ChangedPostPreview: ({ postId, preview }) =>
  postDetails.refetch(model, { postId, preview }),

// Drops one entry without touching siblings. The generation counter is kept.
DismissedPostPreview: ({ postId }) =>
  postDetails.forget(model, { postId }),
```

Refs #1727. This covers its first request, per-key eviction: forget and retainOnly remove KeyedQuery entries, and a Fetch that completes after its entry is removed cannot recreate it.
